.TH FUZZYGENE 1 2000-1月 "fuzzygene_dose_time_surface" "fuzzygene_dose_time_surface"
.SH NAME
fuzzygene_dose_time_surface \- Dose x iteration response surface of one virtual perturbation.
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fIfuzzygene_dose_time_surface(\fBfuzzygene\fR as <generic> FuzzyGeneModel, 
\fBgene\fR as string, 
\fBdoses\fR as double = \fB<NULL>\fR, 
\fBsteps\fR as integer = 60, 
\fBtop\fR as integer = 20, 
[\fB<Environment>\fR]);\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Dose x iteration response surface of one virtual perturbation.
.PP
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
\fBfuzzygene\fB \fR\- a trained (or restored) model. 
.PP
.PP
\fBgene\fB \fR\- the target gene of the virtual perturbation. 
.PP
.PP
\fBdoses\fB \fR\- dose points in [0, 1]; \fBNULL\fR uses 5 evenly spaced points. 
.PP
.PP
\fBsteps\fB \fR\- iteration budget of each solve. 
.PP
.PP
\fBtop\fB \fR\- number of genes to keep. 
.PP
.PP
\fBenv\fB \fR\- the R# runtime environment used to report errors. 
.PP
.SH VALUE
.PP
a long data.frame \fBdose\fR / \fBiteration\fR / \fBgene\fR / \fBdelta\fR
.PP
.SH DETAILS
.PP
Every cell is `mutant(t) - control(t)` at the same frame, i.e. the drift of the system
 itself has already been subtracted. Only the top genes (ranked by \fB|z|\fR at the largest
 dose) are kept, so the cube stays small enough to plot as a contour or a 3D surface.
.PP
.SH SEE ALSO
FuzzyGene
.SH FILES
.PP
biosystem.dll
.PP
